# A `pattern =>` line meant as a lambda in an arm's body starts a new arm
# (`fung fmt` shows it at the arms' indentation): here `y`, which matches
# everything, so the `_` arm never runs. Put a lambda that is the arm's
# value in parentheses.
fn pick(m) = match m:
  1 =>
    print("one")
  y => y + 1
  _ => (y => y)
;;
print(pick(1), pick(2))
# expect-error: E0235
